    docs: require three gates before deployed machine release
    
    Retain every deployed physical machine until its deployed feature lineage is
    integrated into approved defaults, the user accepts the resulting behavior,
    and the user explicitly directs that machine's release. Keep repository
    merge ownership short and feature preparation independent.
    
    Route evidence and release checks through the coordination guide, preserving
    source and migration lineage, actual system/profile identities and original
    recovery contracts. Distinguish legacy automatic lifecycle release behavior
    from permission to perform it. This changes guidance, not lifecycle or claim
    state machines, receipt formats or retained session settings.

